From e0ce59132964392382136eb172b08b337e61ebea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:15:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] S2-10: plat_busy / plat_busy_step hooks in the save
 codec, the load and town_new; golden-bytes and cut-off tests

save_game, load_game and town_new run to the end in one tick (GBA: save 10.7 s, load 6 s, a New story's
town 2 s; the cost is the per-citizen base record the codec and the build rebuild). They now tell the
platform: plat_busy(kind) first, then plat_busy_step(done, total) once per citizen handled (both save
passes, the applying decode, the town build), so a platform can keep a card moving at 30 pictures a second.
Defaults do nothing (plat_weak_ext.c), so the host build and every port that does not use them are unchanged.
load_game only starts it once the slot has a save (a missing save stays a quick "no save").

Tests (core/tests):
- test_busy.c: the hooks are called once per save / load / build, before any step, one step per citizen
  (two passes on the streamed path), done <= total; a missing save starts no card. The streamed save cut
  at the first, second, third, a quarter, half, last-but-one and last write leaves the previous slot
  byte for byte and loading (atomicity, host platform).
- test_save_golden.c: the size and CRC-32 of the image of four deterministic islands, taken on ee686c74
  (before this change): the saved bytes are identical.

Docs for the platform side follow with the GBA / PS1 work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
